      <string id="Ribbon_Explain">Enable any configuration item of this Ribbon, the corresponding Ribbon will be hidden.

Self Category: Enable this configuration item, the whole Tab will be hidden.
SelfPanel: Enable this configuration item, the corresponding panel will be hidden.
Itself: Enable this configuration item, the corresponding button will be hidden.</string>
      <string id="Ribbon_TabElements">TabElements</string>
      <string id="RMS_Add">Add 'protected' to the name of encrypted files</string>
      <string id="RMS_Add_Explain">Enable this option to append (protected) to the end of the file name of encrypted files.</string>
      <string id="RMS_DR">Dynamic Revocation</string>
      <string id="RMS_DR_Explain">Enable this option to turn on the dynamic revocation feature in the client. Please refer to the user manual to configure the web service when trying using this feature.
Revocation is a mechanism that revokes a PDF document that has already been issued. The primary purpose of revocation is to prevent entities that are no longer trusted from participating in an RMS system.</string>
      <string id="RMS_ENCRYPT_METADATA">Encrypt Metadata</string>
      <string id="RMS_EncryptionIntensity_Explain">Enable this option to use deprecated encryption algorithms (RSA 1024 encryption algorithm) to be compatible with the previous version and disable the setting in 'Preferences > RMS Setting'.

If not defined, AD RMS cryptographic implementation, which supports RSA 2048 for encryption, is the default setting.

'RSA 2048 encryption algorithm' requires one of the following operating systems:
1. AD RMS servers: Windows Server</string>
      <string id="RMS_ER">Extended Rights</string>
      <string id="RMS_ER_Explain">Enable this option to turn on the extended rights feature in the client. Please refer to the user manual to configure the web service when using this feature.
Extended rights allow the document owner to control the following items:
Access times: Limit times that users can access a document
Print times: Limit times that users can print a document</string>
      <string id="RMS_Interoperability">RMS Interoperability</string>
      <string id="RMS_Interoperability_Explain">Enable this option, all encrypted PDF will conform to Microsoft IRM Protection for PDF Specification and hence be able to be decrypted by other RMS Viewer. </string>
      <string id="RMS_IRM_Explain">Choose Microsoft IRM Protection Version for document encryption. If not defined, Microsoft IRM Protection V2 is used.</string>
      <string id="RMS_IRMV1">Microsoft IRM Protection</string>
      <string id="RMS_Restricted">Restrict Access</string>
      <string id="RMS_SaveAs">Save As</string>
      <string id="RMS_SaveAs_Explain">Enable this option to turn on the Save As feature for RMS protected files.</string>
      <string id="RMS_SETTING">Rights Management Services</string>
